From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] gpiolib: sysfs: reject export of a number in a chipless
 gpio_device

A gpio_device outlives its gpio_chip while consumers still hold
descriptors: gpiochip_remove() sets gdev->chip to NULL and leaves the
device on gpio_devices with its base/ngpio range intact.  gpio_to_desc()
still resolves a legacy global number inside that range, so
export_store() loads gc = desc->gdev->chip == NULL and passes it to
gpiochip_line_is_valid(), which reads gc->valid_mask and oopses:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at 0x1e0
  pc : gpiochip_line_is_valid+0x0/0x30
  lr : export_store+0x78/0x1b0

Reproduced on 6.1.141-cip43 by unbinding and rebinding gpio-gd32-bridge
(its base moved 394 -> 372, Wi-Fi/BT consumers kept the old device
alive) and writing a number from the old range to /sys/class/gpio/export.

Return -ENODEV when the chip is gone.  The other gdev->chip dereferences
reachable from sysfs are already safe or unreachable with a stale number:

 - unexport_store() only reaches gpiod_free(); gpiod_free_commit() tests
   gc before using it and gpiod_unexport() does not touch the chip.
 - gpiod_export() (called later by export_store) already returns -ENODEV
   for a NULL chip.
 - The per-line attributes (direction/value/edge/...) and the lock_as_irq
   calls in gpio_sysfs_request_irq()/free_irq() only exist for an exported
   line; gpiochip_sysfs_unregister() frees every FLAG_SYSFS descriptor
   before gdev->chip is cleared, and gpiod_export() refuses a chipless
   device, so no such attribute can be reached with a stale number.

This is a minimal local guard, not a backport.  The check-then-use window
between this test and gpiochip_line_is_valid() is not closed here.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local guard; upstream reworked gdev->chip under SRCU]

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-sysfs.c b/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-sysfs.c
index a646486..0c75cc2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-sysfs.c
@@ -447,6 +447,9 @@ static ssize_t export_store(struct class *class,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 	gc = desc->gdev->chip;
+	/* the chip was removed but a consumer keeps its gpio_device alive */
+	if (!gc)
+		return -ENODEV;
 	offset = gpio_chip_hwgpio(desc);
 	if (!gpiochip_line_is_valid(gc, offset)) {
 		pr_warn("%s: GPIO %ld masked\n", __func__, gpio);
